## Issues hit during implementation (and how they were resolved)

### `mkdir` broke existing tests — fixed by adding `mkdir?` to the FileSystem seam
First implementation called `node:fs/promises.mkdir` directly in runInit (ignoring opts.fs). This caused `cli.test.ts` and `integration.test.ts` to fail because those tests pass `InMemoryFs` (which doesn't have a mkdir) and use paths like `/data` that the real filesystem rejects (`EACCES` creating `/data` at root). Fix: add `mkdir?` as an OPTIONAL method to `FileSystem`; runInit calls `opts.fs.mkdir` only when present. In-memory fakes skip the mkdir; production fs implements it. New `HybridFs` in `cli-init.test.ts` combines in-memory files + real mkdir for the boundary test.

### `unknown` type errored on check-banned-types
`lifecycle.ts:readPidFile` initially cast the JSON.parse result as `{pid?: unknown; dataDir?: unknown; startedAt?: unknown}`. The repo's check-banned-types script rejects `unknown`. Fix: typed as `{pid?: string | number; dataDir?: string; startedAt?: string}`.

### Dist build initially didn't include the new code
The bundled CLI uses `bin.bundled.cjs` (built from `bin.ts` via esbuild). After editing `cli.ts`, `pnpm --filter @spanexx/agentide build` rebuilt the dist. The init still failed on the real binary until I added `mkdir` to `bin.ts`'s `defaultFs` separately — `bin.ts` doesn't import `nodeFileSystem` from gateway-core, it has its own minimal fs implementation. **The integration of gateway-core's `nodeFileSystem` was never used by the bundled CLI before this pack.** That's why both `factory.ts` and `bin.ts` needed updating independently.

### `--help` gate at the top level swallowed `client grant --help`
First Phase 4 implementation: `runClient` checks `flags["help"]`, but `runCli`'s top-level gate (L231: `if (cmd === undefined || cmd === "--help" || cmd === "-h" || flags["help"] === true)`) short-circuited before `runClient` ran. `agentide client grant --help` printed the full top-level help instead of the grant-specific help. Fix: only short-circuit top-level when `cmd === undefined`. Then `agentide client grant --help` reaches `runClient`, sees `flags.help === true`, prints grant help.

### File corruption from edit_file JSON escaping
Several times during Phase 4 my `edit_file` calls with complex multi-line template literals got mangled (literal `\n` in source instead of newlines, broken syntax). Recovered each time with a Node one-liner via `terminal` that spliced the corrupted block with proper newlines. The file `packages/agentide/src/cli.ts` is clean now — last validation was a successful `pnpm --filter @spanexx/agentide build`.

